/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Modern HPC centers typically prefer batch scheduling to share resources fairly across users and projects. SLURM, an open-source scheduler, enforces resource quotas and walltime limits per job. This is beneficial for throughput and fairness, but introduces friction for stateful or interactive workloads inside VMs that are not naturally checkpoint/restart friendly.)
/E (Modern HPC centers typically prefer batch scheduling to share resources fairly across users and projects. SLURM, an open-source scheduler, enforces resource quotas and walltime limits per job. This is beneficial for throughput and fairness, but introduces friction for stateful or interactive workloads inside VMs that are not naturally checkpoint/restart friendly.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
