/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The broader implications are significant. This approach allows researchers to maintain persistent development environments, interactive workflows, and stateful services on a cluster designed  for batch computation. It also establishes a repeatable pattern for running long-lived virtualized workloads in scheduled compute environments, offering a foundation for future enhancements such as automated health checks, improved scheduling logic, or integration with container-based systems.)
/E (The broader implications are significant. This approach allows researchers to maintain persistent development environments, interactive workflows, and stateful services on a cluster designed  for batch computation. It also establishes a repeatable pattern for running long-lived virtualized workloads in scheduled compute environments, offering a foundation for future enhancements such as automated health checks, improved scheduling logic, or integration with container-based systems.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In summary, the recursive migration framework provides a practical, policy-aligned method for sustaining VMs indefinitely on HPC infrastructure. It solves a longstanding operational challenge while remaining simple to maintain and adaptable to other clusters or research workflows.)
/E (In summary, the recursive migration framework provides a practical, policy-aligned method for sustaining VMs indefinitely on HPC infrastructure. It solves a longstanding operational challenge while remaining simple to maintain and adaptable to other clusters or research workflows.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
